thag6.3:1.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:1.2 starts: is not found,
thag6.3:1.3 starts: wastes away from the True Dhamma
thag6.3:1.4 starts: like a fish in next to no water.
thag6.3:2.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:2.2 starts: is not found,
thag6.3:2.3 starts: doesn’t grow in the True Dhamma,
thag6.3:2.4 starts: like a rotten seed in a field.
thag6.3:3.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:3.2 starts: is not found,
thag6.3:3.3 starts: is far away from unbinding
thag6.3:3.4 starts: in the teaching of the Dhamma king.
thag6.3:4.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:4.2 starts: is found,
thag6.3:4.3 starts: doesn’t waste away from the True Dhamma
thag6.3:4.4 starts: like a fish in plentiful water.
thag6.3:5.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:5.2 starts: is found,
thag6.3:5.3 starts: grows in the True Dhamma,
thag6.3:5.4 starts: like an excellent seed in a field.
thag6.3:6.1 starts: One in whom respect for his fellows in
thag6.3:6.2 starts: is found,
thag6.3:6.3 starts: stands right in the presence of unbinding
thag6.3:6.4 starts: in the teaching of the Dhamma king.
thag6.6:1.1 starts: Twenty five years since my going forth,
thag6.6:1.2 starts: and no peace of awareness
thag6.6:1.3 starts: —not a finger-snap’s worth—
thag6.6:1.4 starts: attained.
thag6.6:4.1 starts: So, taking a razor,
thag6.6:4.2 starts: I sat down on a bed.
thag6.6:4.3 starts: And there was the razor,
thag6.6:4.4 starts: placed ready to cut my own vein,
thag6.10:1.1 starts: When I was seven
thag6.10:1.2 starts: & newly gone forth,
thag6.10:1.3 starts: having conquered with my power
thag6.10:1.4 starts: the great powerful serpent,
thag6.12:3.1 starts: You live for the good of both
thag6.12:3.2 starts: —your own, the other’s—
thag6.12:3.3 starts: when, knowing the other’s provoked,
thag6.12:3.4 starts: you mindfully grow calm.
thag7.1:5.1 starts: And seeing her before me—
thag7.1:5.2 starts: a courtesan, ornamented, finely clothed,
thag7.1:5.3 starts: hands palm-to-palm over her heart—
thag7.1:5.4 starts: like a snare of death laid out,
thag5.10:5.1 starts: But whoever hears the Conqueror’s teaching
thag5.10:5.2 starts: with guarded intent,
thag5.10:5.3 starts: doing away with effluents
thag5.10:5.4 starts: realizing the unshakable,
thag5.10:5.5 starts: attaining the foremost peace,
thag5.10:5.6 starts: —effluent-free—
thag6.5:4.1 starts: To all of you gathered here
thag6.5:4.2 starts: Good fortune.
thag6.5:4.3 starts: Dig up craving
thag6.5:4.4 starts: —as when seeking medicinal roots, wild grass—
thag6.5:4.5 starts: Don’t let Māra cut you down
thag6.5:4.6 starts: —as a raging river, a reed—
thag6.6:5.1 starts: when apt attention arose in me,
thag6.6:5.2 starts: the drawbacks appeared,
thag6.6:5.3 starts: disenchantment stood
thag6.6:5.4 starts: at an even keel:
thag6.9:1.1 starts: I was
thag6.9:1.2 starts: wealth, & sovereignty.
thag6.9:1.3 starts: Drunk with the intoxication
thag6.9:1.4 starts: I wandered about,
thag6.9:2.1 starts: regarding no one
thag6.9:2.2 starts: as my equal or better.
thag6.9:2.3 starts: Foolish, arrogant,
thag6.9:2.4 starts: haughty,
thag6.9:3.1 starts: I—disrespectful, arrogant, proud—
thag6.9:3.2 starts: bowed down to no one,
thag6.9:3.3 starts: not even
thag6.9:3.4 starts: or those commonly held
thag6.12:2.1 starts: You make things worse
thag6.12:2.2 starts: when you flare up
thag6.12:2.3 starts: Whoever doesn’t flare up
thag6.12:2.4 starts: wins a battle
thag6.13:6.1 starts: Your last day approaches.
thag6.13:6.2 starts: This isn’t your time
# superseded: thag6.13:6.3 starts: to be heedless.
# superseded: thag6.13:6.4 none
thag7.1:2.1 starts: Stepping out of her slippers—
thag7.1:2.2 starts: her hands raised before me,
thag7.1:2.3 starts: she softly, tenderly,
thag7.1:2.4 starts: spoke to me first:
thag7.1:6.1 starts: apt attention arose in me,
thag7.1:6.2 starts: the drawbacks appeared,
thag7.1:6.3 starts: disenchantment stood
thag7.1:6.4 starts: at an even keel:
